    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alzheimer&apos;s disease with early onset (G30.0)</content>. Donepezil 5 mg tolerated for five weeks; pulse 64. [S]<list><item>Donepezil 10 mg at bedtime.</item><item>Call for nausea, loose stools, dizziness or a pulse below 55.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Type 2 diabetes (E11.9)</content>. Hemoglobin A1c 6.9% off glipizide, within his goal of under 8.0%, with no low readings. [S]<list><item>Continue metformin.</item><item>Hemoglobin A1c in six months.</item><item>Eye examination re-booked with paratransit and a same-morning reminder call to his care partner.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive testing (MoCA, MMSE)</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly, or sooner with change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Next in a year</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medicine review for anticholinergic and sedating drugs (Beers)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No anticholinergic or sedating drugs</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Behavioral and psychological symptoms (NPI-Q items)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Cholinesterase inhibitor: benefit, nausea, diarrhea, dreams, pulse</td><td>Each follow-up and each dose change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Five weeks on 5 mg without side effects; pulse 64; raised to 10 mg today</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Driving, firearm and home safety</td><td>At diagnosis and each follow-up</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Not driving; no firearm in the home; stove shut-off fitted</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Care partner support and burden (Zarit, narrative)</td><td>At diagnosis, then at least yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Adult day program two days a week; caregiver class started</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning</td><td>At diagnosis; revisit yearly and at changes</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Completed at the preventive visit two weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Hemoglobin A1c, goal under 8.0% for an older adult with cognitive impairment, and hypoglycemia review</td><td>Every three months after a therapy change; every six months when stable</td><td>Completed today</td><td>6.9%, from 6.4%, off glipizide; no low readings</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure, goal under 130/80 mmHg</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>128/76 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Potassium and creatinine on lisinopril and metformin</td><td>Yearly, and after acute illness or dehydration</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Dilated diabetic eye examination</td><td>Every one to two years without retinopathy</td><td>Deferred</td><td>The dilated eye examination requested at intake was missed because he no longer drives and the appointment was forgotten on the morning. No harm is known: he has no visual symptoms and his diabetes is well controlled, but retinopathy cannot be excluded until he is examined. Corrective action: re-booked with paratransit, a same-morning reminder call to his care partner, and the appointment added to the day program&apos;s calendar</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exercise and social activity</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Day program exercise group and daily walks</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Find the cause of the memory loss and explain it to him in a way he can take in. Outcome by 2026-08-18: Alzheimer&apos;s disease confirmed by amyloid PET; disclosed with his care partner present, at his request, with written notes [S]</item><item>No hypoglycemia, with hemoglobin A1c under 8.0%. In progress; target 2026-10-27 [S]</item><item>Stay safe: no driving and no firearm in the home. Outcome by 2026-08-18: He stopped driving and the handgun was removed from the home [S]</item><item>Keep his days full and give his care partner regular breaks. In progress; target 2026-10-27 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tdap vaccine, deferred from the preventive visit at his request [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD): Executive summary of recommendations for specialty care (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Alzheimer&apos;s disease, diabetes type 2 and hypertension monographs (2026); 13. Older Adults: Standards of Care in Diabetes-2026 (2026); American Geriatrics Society 2023 updated AGS Beers Criteria for potentially inappropriate medication use in older adults (2023); Practice Parameter update: Evaluation and management of driving risk in dementia (2010); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Tdap given today. Eye examination as re-booked. Sixteen-week review in five weeks. Call for side effects of the higher donepezil dose. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-27: sixteen-week review: medicines, kidneys, mood, caregiver strain and the plan. [S]</paragraph></text>

